# Template for the local .env. Copy to .env and fill in.
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# .env is gitignored. This file is the committed template and must never
# contain a real value.
#
# What is NOT here, deliberately: authority-level, authority_ceiling, and
# pipeline-kill-switch live in config/capabilities.yaml and are committed.
# Changing what the system is permitted to do has to show up in git log
# (design.md section 6.5), so they are never environment variables.


# --- Build order step 2 -----------------------------------------------------

# LaunchDarkly SERVER-side SDK key. Starts with "sdk-".
# Not the client-side ID and not a mobile key — the server SDK rejects those.
# Keys are scoped per LD environment; use a test-environment key while
# building. Covers both flag evaluation and AI Config (agent instruction)
# retrieval — there is no second LD credential.
LD_SDK_KEY=


# --- Build order step 3 -----------------------------------------------------

# Shippo API token. A test token is all this project needs: it quotes rates and
# validates addresses, and never buys a label. Dispatch was removed (design 9),
# so nothing here can spend money whichever token you supply.
#
# Covers two things the spine currently fabricates: rate quotes for C5, and
# the transit estimates C3 gates on. Design 5 lists transit duration as the one
# externally-supplied planning input, and design 4 uses Shippo for B2 address
# validation, so this is one credential for all three.
#
# Without it `run plan` stops. There is deliberately no fallback: an invented
# rate produces a plausible-looking total on a manifest a human is about to
# approve, which is worse than no manifest at all.
SHIPPO_API_KEY=


# --- Agents (D1 today) ------------------------------------------------------

# Anthropic API key, for the model the agent runs on. Billed against prepaid
# credits at console.anthropic.com — a Claude subscription does not cover it.
#
# Which model is called is not set here. LaunchDarkly serves it as part of the
# AI Config, along with the instruction text and the model parameters
# (design 6.1), so switching models is a console edit rather than a deploy.
#
# Needed only when `verification-enabled` is on. With it off, D1 is skipped and
# the run hands over a manually reviewed manifest — design 6.10's normal path,
# less helpful and not less correct.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
